        <p>The Examiner Saturday, July 11, 1903.</p>
        <p>FASHIONS OF TO-DAY.</p>
        <p>The weather so far this summer has be so fickle and variable that . one is at a lose to know what to wear or how best to advise those who are in doubt as to what they shall select, Still, with hope ever green in our hearts, we feel confident in recommending the selection of some of the very charming materials which this season has brought, Black and white is a combination which has for the last two summers met with the ap- proval of the best dressed women who are even in the van of fashion, and its charms ;eem to be now more than ever emphasised .13r the doubtful character. A toilette of this .iescription will look nice and in keeping with</p>
        <p>. ›`• • gri • • • • tfib, : • -•:.- •. , I, s.' $4 ~ . i 4(l\\ ,</p>
