      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1903-07-11_WidnesExaminer_art0131" n="art0131">
        <head>LIFE STORIES ILLUSTRATED.</head>
        <p>LIFE STORIES ILLUSTRATED.</p>
        <p>A Cigar Store Salesman.</p>
        <p>In theGREAT CAMPAIGNS OF COMMERCE, he most distinguished BUSINESS MENowe their prominence to that Untiring Energy and Dominant Mental Activity which irresistibly impels its possessirs to attain the very Zenith of Success. In the ceaseless endeavour to wrest aCompetency from the VICISSITUDES OF TRADEeveryNerve and Faculty is strained to its utmost capacity, and whenCLE VER MEN fail, their mystify' ng collapse is due, more often than is suspected, to the severe tax which Modern Enterprises impose upon their Physical Resources, rendering them unable to take advantage of the Opportunities which their energy has created. The Happy Experience of the Business Man -</p>
        <p>whose letter-is published below, makes it Clear that under such unfavourable circumstances it is yet possible for anyone to recover their Natural Vigour and renew their Vitality by a recourse to the recuperative properties of Phosferinc..</p>
